1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,500
NUBI: [hero line from the chosen beat 2 take, e.g. "That's the power button,
the red one at the top."]

2
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:10,500
NARRATOR: One in four Americans
65 and older lives alone.

3
00:00:10,700 --> 00:00:17,000
When a new remote or a coffee machine gets the better of them,
there's nobody in the room to ask.

4
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:21,500
NUBI: [greeting as spoken in the take]

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:26,000
USER: Nubi, come here.

6
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:28,000
NUBI: On my way!

7
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:41,000
[Nubi walks around the sofa and stops in front of you]

8
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:45,000
NARRATOR: Hold something up, point at it, and ask.

9
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:47,500
USER: What is this?

10
00:00:48,500 --> 00:01:03,000
NUBI: [answer about the remote as spoken in the take]

11
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:07,000
USER: Which button turns it on?

12
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:18,000
NUBI: [power button answer as spoken in the take]

13
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:26,000
[presses the button: the TV comes on]

14
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:31,500
USER: Follow me.

15
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:33,500
NUBI: [reply as spoken in the take]

16
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:39,000
NARRATOR: Ask it to follow, and it walks with you,
around your real furniture.

17
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:43,000
USER: Stop.

18
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:45,000
NUBI: [reply as spoken in the take, if any]

19
00:01:47,500 --> 00:01:50,000
USER: Tell me everything about this remote.

20
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:55,500
NUBI: [answer as spoken in the take, up to the pinch]

21
00:01:55,500 --> 00:01:57,000
[pinch: Nubi stops mid-sentence and listens]

22
00:01:57,500 --> 00:01:59,000
USER: That's enough, thanks.

23
00:01:59,500 --> 00:02:01,500
NUBI: [reply as spoken in the take]

24
00:02:02,500 --> 00:02:05,500
NARRATOR: When the network drops, Nubi doesn't go silent.

25
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:07,500
[hotspot off]

26
00:02:08,500 --> 00:02:09,500
USER: Are you there?

27
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:15,000
NUBI: [offline line as spoken in the take, e.g.
"I can't reach the internet right now, but I'm still here with you."]

28
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:17,000
[hotspot on]

29
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:20,500
USER: Thanks, Nubi. See you later!

30
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:24,000
NUBI: [online reply as spoken in the take]

31
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:28,000
NARRATOR: For anyone at home with nobody to ask.

32
00:02:28,200 --> 00:02:34,500
Nubi is open source, built on Muse Spark,
SAM 3.1 and Muse Voice Transcribe.
